.TH GETHOSTBYNAME 3
.SH NAME
gethostbyname, gethostbyaddr, gethostent, sethostent, endhostent \- IPv4 host lookup
.SH SYNOPSIS
#include <netdb.h>
.SH DESCRIPTION
gethostbyname searches DNS with resolver(3); gethostbyaddr performs an
in-addr.arpa PTR lookup for a four-byte AF_INET address. Only ECONNREFUSED
permits fallback to hosts(5). Timeouts, NXDOMAIN and NODATA do not use hosts.
All-digit/dot names without a final dot use inet_aton without DNS.
.PP
Returned hostent storage is static and non-reentrant. Addresses are aligned
four-byte network-order values. Up to 35 addresses and 35 CNAME aliases are
returned. CNAME chains may appear out of order; cycles and malformed records
fail with NO_RECOVERY. No matching address yields NO_DATA.
.PP
gethostent iterates /etc/hosts. sethostent rewinds it; a nonzero argument also
sets RES_USEVC and RES_STAYOPEN. endhostent closes the file and resolver TCP
connection and clears those flags. Lookup failure returns NULL and sets
h_errno; use herror or hstrerror to describe it. No IPv6 support is included.
